# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=skyward spec=druid:guardian style=melee
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
# `boss=skyward` is a coverage label only (direction.md's 2026-09-25/26
# notes on playpick.ts): a mode=walk evening steers at no named boss, the
# walk starts at the door same as any other.
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (the 2026-09-26-40.play recipe),
# rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: druid:guardian (sessions.jsonl, five
# priors: mode=clear wander/flee/good, mode=walk boss=confluence good,
# mode=battleground mash) has never been given `style=melee`, and has never
# run mode=walk at 25-heroic -- its one prior mode=walk reading was
# 10-normal/good. `melee` closes to the boss and never leaves regardless of
# what is on the floor (scripts/playbot.ts:952-954, the same policy that
# made #267's bonestorm complaint and the Bloodgorged-tank wipe above), which
# for once matches the role: guardian is a tank, and a tank standing in melee
# and never disengaging is closer to correct play than it was for the priest
# and warlock this style has already been run on. The open question is
# whether a tank spec's own kit (self-healing, mitigation) covers for
# `melee`'s refusal to ever step out of a hazard the way it did not for a
# healer or a caster dps, across a full evening's worth of corridors and
# fights rather than one isolated pull.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:druid:guardian
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening melee 240 6
state
shot end
says
bill
